A vault whose marker watermark trails the shipped migrations still gets the session-start block
from the hook — the playbook table — plus one line pointing at `migrate`, never the migrate gate's
auto-migrate notice: at session start there is no request to resume after a migration.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 2
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/config.yaml --
-- cmd --
sh -c 'root=$(dirname "$(dirname "$(command -v booping)")"); CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT=$root "$root/hooks/session-start.sh" | grep -E "^(## booping|\| (Playbook|migrate) |This vault|\*\*)"'
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
## booping
| Playbook | Trigger |
| migrate | a render surface reports the vault is behind and tells the user to run `/playbook migrate`; an explicit ask to migrate or update a vault |
This vault is behind on booping migrations; `/booping:playbook migrate` brings it up to date.
-- stderr --
